            <description>Prolonged (up to 20s) rhythmical sharp or spiky activity over the frontal areas (maximum over the frontal midline) seen at arousal from sleep in children with minimal cerebral dysfunction. (Source: Beniczky ea 2013, Appendix S6; Beniczky ea 2017, Table 14.)</description>
